    "result_text": "All tests pass. The build is green with the full suite (the only runnable test is `AcceptanceTest`; `AcceptanceBase` is abstract and `AuditLogCapture` is a helper).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented shared-household support for `POST /api/owners`. When a request sets `sharesHousehold: true` and an owner with the same last name and address already exists, the join is allowed and both owners are given the same stable `householdId`, which is now returned.\n\n**Design** \u2014 kept each concern in its own small unit and reused logic rather than duplicating it:\n\n- **`Households`** (new package-private helper) \u2014 the single home for household logic: `normalize()` (case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed), `membersOf(...)` (existing owners in the same household), and `idFor(...)` (a **stable** identifier derived deterministically as a SHA-256 prefix of the normalized last name + address, so every member computes the same value with no coordination).\n- **`EnsureUniqueHousehold`** \u2014 refactored to delegate its matching to `Households.membersOf(...)` instead of carrying its own copy of the normalize/match code. Behavior unchanged: rejects a non-sharing duplicate with 409; skips when `sharesHousehold` is true.\n- **`AssignHouseholdId`** (new pipeline step) \u2014 when opted in and a matching owner exists, sets the shared `householdId` on the new owner and back-fills it onto existing members (persisting only those that change). Runs after `BuildOwner`/`AssignOwnerCustomerCode` and before `SaveOwner`, under `transaction` governance.\n\n**Supporting changes:**\n- `Owner` model \u2014 added the `householdId` field (`household_id` column) with getter/setter.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added `householdId` as a read-only string on the `Owner` schema (regenerates `OwnerDto`; MapStruct maps it automatically, so both the create response and `GET` expose it).\n- `schema.sql` for all four platforms (hsqldb \u2014 used by tests \u2014 plus h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `household_id` column.\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 wired the `assignHouseholdId` step into the pipeline.",
